# C++ Component Rules

## ISR / threading — most critical constraint

`LinBusListener::onReceive_()` and `read_lin_frame_()` run in an interrupt or a dedicated FreeRTOS task (core 0). You **must not** call `ESP_LOG*` from that context; it is not ISR-safe.

```cpp
// ❌ BAD — direct ESP_LOG inside ISR or event-task
ESP_LOGW(TAG, "CRC error");

// ✅ GOOD — enqueue a typed log message, drain it on the main task
QUEUE_LOG_MSG log_msg = QUEUE_LOG_MSG();
log_msg.type = QUEUE_LOG_MSG_TYPE::WARN_READ_LIN_FRAME_LINv1_CRC;
TRUMA_LOGW_ISR(log_msg);           // queue-based, ISR-safe
// then in process_log_queue(): ESP_LOGW(TAG, …)
```

Macros: `TRUMA_LOGE_ISR`, `TRUMA_LOGW_ISR`, `TRUMA_LOGI_ISR`, `TRUMA_LOGV_ISR`, `TRUMA_LOGVV_ISR` (defined in `LinBusLog.h`). The non-`_ISR` variants (`TRUMA_LOGE`, etc.) are for main-task use only.

## Naming — enforced by `.clang-tidy`

| Symbol | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Class / Struct / Enum | `CamelCase` | `LinBusListener`, `QUEUE_LIN_MSG` |
| Enum constants | `UPPER_CASE` | `HEATING_MODE_ECO` |
| Public / protected member variables | `lower_case_` (trailing `_`) | `lin_checksum_` |
| Private member variables | `lower_case_` (trailing `_`) | `fault_on_lin_bus_reported_` |
| Methods (all visibility) | `lower_case` | `answer_lin_order_` |
| Local variables / parameters | `lower_case` | `data_length` |
| `static const char *const TAG` | `UPPER_CASE` variable name | `TAG` |

## Platform `#ifdef` splits

```cpp
#ifdef USE_ESP32_FRAMEWORK_ARDUINO
  // Arduino-specific setup (hw_serial->onReceive, xTaskCreatePinnedToCore)
#endif
#ifdef USE_ESP32_FRAMEWORK_ESP_IDF
  // IDF-specific (uart_event_t queue)
#endif
#ifdef USE_RP2040
  // RP2040 hardware UART + FreeRTOS
#endif
```

Never mix platform logic in `LinBusListener.cpp`; it must stay in the platform-specific files.

## Formatting

- Column limit: **120** (`.clang-format`).
- Indent: **2 spaces**, never tabs.
- Run `clang-format` before committing.

## FreeRTOS queues

Queues (`lin_msg_queue_`, `log_queue_`) use **static storage** — do not replace with dynamic `xQueueCreate`. Queue lengths are controlled by `TRUMA_MSG_QUEUE_LENGTH` and `TRUMA_LOG_QUEUE_LENGTH` preprocessor defines.
